# Kotlin
.kotlin/

# Android
local.properties
captures/
# Signing keys never enter the repository — the release workflow decodes one from a secret into
# the runner's temp directory. This is the net under that rule, not the rule itself.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Sign-in credentials, for the same reason one line up. Each of these is a one-shot download —
# Apple's `.p8` cannot be downloaded twice and a Google client secret is shown once — so a commit
# that reached this public repository would be answered by revoking the credential, not by
# rewriting history: GitHub keeps unreachable commits reachable by SHA, and forks keep their own.
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
client_secret*.json
.env
.env.*

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# Xcode
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

